        <title>Flats_MarineSwamps</title>
        <abstract>All features have been included from the Surface Hydrology data capture. 250K Specification Description - Marine Swamp - That low lying part of the backshore area of tidal waters, usually immediately behind saline coastal flat, which maintains a high salt water content, and is covered with characteristic thick grasses and reed growths. (Source - http://www.ga.gov.au/mapspecs/topographic/v6/appendixA_files/Waterbodies.html)</abstract>
